00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:56.750
&gt;&gt; You are responsible for
sustainability for the group.

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:58.550
What does that mean for Jumia?

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.552
And what are some of the key
initiatives that you're focused on or

00:18:01.552 --> 00:18:05.170
the organization is focused on
in the sustainability space?

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:06.600
&gt;&gt; The first thing for

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:13.010
us is actually very clear validation
that our mission itself is sustainable.

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:18.400
We don't have to invent some
new projects to go after.

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:22.951
I mean it doesn't mean, of course we would
have to operate in a sustainable manner,

00:18:22.951 --> 00:18:27.117
reducing in terms of our shipments,
reducing use of packaging materials and

00:18:27.117 --> 00:18:27.710
all that.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:32.585
So all of those are very important hygiene
factors which we build into our day to day

00:18:32.585 --> 00:18:34.110
operation.

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:38.786
But just realizing that our mission,
which is about in the end,

00:18:38.786 --> 00:18:43.375
when you look at is about reducing
inequality is so critical and

00:18:43.375 --> 00:18:49.264
is a big part of how we create value, and
how we create sustainable improvement,

00:18:49.264 --> 00:18:52.670
and quality of lives on the continent.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:57.060
And asking ourselves what more
can we do with that mission?

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:01.519
And second part of it is that
we have a full ecosystem of many

00:19:01.519 --> 00:19:06.615
partners that working together can
actually create more value for

00:19:06.615 --> 00:19:10.960
the communities that we live
in than just Jumia itself.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.235
We have sellers,
we have third party logistics partners,

00:19:14.235 --> 00:19:16.310
we have brands who work with us.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:20.537
So that's a full ecosystem that if we
deploy can actually do a lot more for

00:19:20.537 --> 00:19:22.370
sustainability.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:27.239
So that's our focus, and that's our
area of attention for this first year.

00:19:27.239 --> 00:19:32.279
I mean, this is the first year that we're
actually putting together our practices,

00:19:32.279 --> 00:19:35.989
what we're doing and
we would have our first report next year.

00:19:35.989 --> 00:19:41.088
A very practical example is how many
sellers on Jumia are classified as SMEs,

00:19:41.088 --> 00:19:44.069
how many sellers on Jumia
have been able to get

00:19:44.069 --> 00:19:48.480
access to working capital loans
to grow their businesses?

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:50.500
How many sellers on Jumia are women,

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:54.478
how many of them have utilized
the training facilities that we provide,

00:19:54.478 --> 00:19:59.460
how many of them have utilized the loans
to be able to grow their businesses?

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.540
Those are huge,

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:06.150
huge areas of sustainability that we
haven't even scratched all of it right.

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:08.756
Let's utilize what we have first and

00:20:08.756 --> 00:20:13.390
then there are all the levers of
which we can also concentrate on.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.420
So those are some examples for you there.

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:19.940
&gt;&gt; There's a great question here.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:23.860
I'm going to jump in on this one because
this is actually direction I wanted to go.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:27.190
How does Jumia evaluate markets for
potential entry?

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:30.300
And do you ever decide
markets are no longer viable?

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.621
The person who's asking this question
mentions that you may have pulled out of

00:20:33.621 --> 00:20:34.840
Cameroon.

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.950
I want to tack on my own question to that.

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:40.792
You mentioned you're in 11 countries,
500 million people and counting for

00:20:40.792 --> 00:20:44.150
some enormous percentage of
the total GDP on the continent.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:47.758
Can you go to this question and talk a
little bit about the barriers to regional

00:20:47.758 --> 00:20:50.940
expansion and what you look for
when you pick a new country to enter?

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:55.325
&gt;&gt; The question that was actually right
yeah, we had to pull out of Cameroon.

00:20:55.325 --> 00:20:58.642
Remember there was a time when Cameroon
the internet was shut down for

00:20:58.642 --> 00:20:59.920
almost a whole year.

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:00.910
Okay?

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:04.050
These are very important
factors that we look at.

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:07.110
We look at the state of the economy.

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:11.060
We look at beyond GDP,
beyond economic factors.

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:16.650
We're also looking at readiness for
an internet based business like ours.

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:21.302
So those are very important nuances
that we consider in terms of looking at

00:21:21.302 --> 00:21:22.135
expansion.

00:21:22.135 --> 00:21:26.816
For now we're deepening our footprint
within the countries that we are in,

00:21:26.816 --> 00:21:31.645
maybe in the future, but they're certainly
for this year where we're really

00:21:31.645 --> 00:21:35.845
concentrating on those 11 countries
where we're currently in.

00:21:35.845 --> 00:21:40.985
All said and done, we are the largest
E-commerce platform on the continent but

00:21:40.985 --> 00:21:45.741
also in a continent where E-commerce and
I would say all of modern trade is

00:21:45.741 --> 00:21:50.150
probably still within the ranks
of 2 to 5% of total retail.

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:52.810
So you still have a huge upside huge,
huge upside.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:57.789
So before it's up tinkering with
all kinds of categories and

00:21:57.789 --> 00:22:02.961
new verticals and so on,
just given that alone is a significant

00:22:02.961 --> 00:22:06.980
area to focus on, and
that's what our focus is.

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:11.531
And I think the other thing we are
focusing on as well is really the shift

00:22:11.531 --> 00:22:14.852
that consumers have made
from using E-commerce,

00:22:14.852 --> 00:22:19.713
coming to Jumia to buy the electronics,
they wanted to buy products of high

00:22:19.713 --> 00:22:23.417
value because they could get it
at a good price on Jumia and

00:22:23.417 --> 00:22:28.470
they could get quality assurance and
all of that to their everyday products.

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:34.358
So people want to buy food, people want to
buy essential items, home cleaning agents,

00:22:34.358 --> 00:22:39.185
beauty and perfumes, consumables
basically that's a huge shift and

00:22:39.185 --> 00:22:42.899
that's where we are also
deepening our presence in.

00:22:42.899 --> 00:22:46.470
&gt;&gt; I want to go to your competitive
landscape in a second, but I want to pause

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:50.830
and talk about consumables because one of
the things that makes consumables possible

00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:54.630
here in the United States is that
you can get it tomorrow, right?

00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:56.621
You can get your vegetables,
they're still fresh,

00:22:56.621 --> 00:22:58.090
they're maybe even cold packs right?

00:22:58.090 --> 00:23:01.800
You need a toilet roll, you need
cleaning products, whatever it is.

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:02.946
Is that a big deal,

00:23:02.946 --> 00:23:08.600
is that important to your consumers that
they get something really fast or not yet?

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:14.156
&gt;&gt; Yeah, there's always a trade off,
sometimes it's the consumers

00:23:14.156 --> 00:23:19.085
living environment that flows
into their expectations.

00:23:19.085 --> 00:23:19.855
Okay?

00:23:19.855 --> 00:23:23.569
So because in the States
right next to corner,

00:23:23.569 --> 00:23:27.284
there's either Kroger or
there's a Target or

00:23:27.284 --> 00:23:33.185
there's a Wegmans or any other brand
that you can pop into and buy.

00:23:33.185 --> 00:23:37.650
So that flows into consumer
expectations of when do I want it?

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:38.988
I want it like in 10 minutes.

00:23:38.988 --> 00:23:43.330
Of course you can use Instacart as well
and you get the product very quickly.

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:48.172
In our environment is slightly different,
consumers are making trade offs and for

00:23:48.172 --> 00:23:51.920
them it probably the pricing
is more important.

00:23:51.920 --> 00:23:56.124
&gt;&gt; So I got the perfect question here for
you that just follows on this, as part of

00:23:56.124 --> 00:24:00.392
your impact goals that should be, do you
have any special role in supporting or

00:24:00.392 --> 00:24:05.090
facilitating local manufacturing in
the countries where you operate?

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:07.554
We work very closely with brands, so

00:24:07.554 --> 00:24:10.817
we have several brands
that are listed on Jumia.

00:24:10.817 --> 00:24:17.705
And we see an increasing interest from
brands to be on Jumia for many reasons,.

00:24:17.705 --> 00:24:20.934
One being of course,
that it gives an opportunity for

00:24:20.934 --> 00:24:24.826
them to go direct to the consumer,
through Jumia as a platform.

00:24:24.826 --> 00:24:30.252
Two it gives them very useful consumer
insight, and a lot of that consumer

00:24:30.252 --> 00:24:35.430
insight is in terms of packaging in
terms of product specifications.

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:39.380
All of that is useful for
a manufacturer in development and

00:24:39.380 --> 00:24:42.210
product development and, production.

00:24:42.210 --> 00:24:45.415
So the answer is yes,
local manufacturers find,

00:24:45.415 --> 00:24:50.318
being on Jumia extremely useful for
their demand planning and production.

00:24:50.318 --> 00:24:54.317
[MUSIC]

00:24:54.317 --> 00:24:56.995
&gt;&gt; Let's pivot a little bit
to the competitive landscape,

00:24:56.995 --> 00:24:58.291
who are your competitors?

00:24:58.291 --> 00:25:02.909
Is it kong.com or take a lot,
other e-commerce companies that

00:25:02.909 --> 00:25:06.852
are in the continent or,
is Amazon a threat from afar?

00:25:06.852 --> 00:25:09.950
&gt;&gt; I think when you look at
it at the end of the day,

00:25:09.950 --> 00:25:13.970
competition is more the,
