payments and all of that.

00:28:15.602 --> 00:28:20.982
So, there's a whole lot, there's riding or
just completing the purchase

00:28:20.982 --> 00:28:26.529
online that consumers like the option
of having someone, the intermediary,

00:28:26.529 --> 00:28:31.506
the platform that is taking some of
those responsibilities for them.

00:28:31.506 --> 00:28:35.058
&gt;&gt; One of the biggest hurdles for
any e-commerce company,

00:28:35.058 --> 00:28:39.572
is building trust that if I give you
my money, you'll send the product.

00:28:39.572 --> 00:28:43.975
This is especially true in markets where
those online buying habits haven't been

00:28:43.975 --> 00:28:45.073
well established.

00:28:45.073 --> 00:28:50.431
I asked Juliet, what has Jumia done to
create trust with buyers and sellers?

00:28:50.431 --> 00:28:54.800
&gt;&gt; For any market place of course you
would have issues sometimes with sellers

00:28:54.800 --> 00:28:56.129
and so on and so forth.

00:28:56.129 --> 00:28:59.892
But like you mentioned,
we do have recourse mechanisms.

00:28:59.892 --> 00:29:04.199
We have penalties, we score sellers
by many things by speed of delivery,

00:29:04.199 --> 00:29:05.796
by the quality of the item,

00:29:05.796 --> 00:29:09.950
by the return rate of the items
that they sell on the platform.

00:29:09.950 --> 00:29:12.086
So, many things are built into it,

00:29:12.086 --> 00:29:15.490
and of course we have seven
items which must be Q seed.

00:29:15.490 --> 00:29:17.644
We have manufacturer warranties and

00:29:17.644 --> 00:29:21.819
we offer everything that you can
think of from a recourse perspective.

00:29:21.819 --> 00:29:26.181
And for some of our consumers also
depending on the type of item and

00:29:26.181 --> 00:29:29.608
the specific consumers
behavior on our platform.

00:29:29.608 --> 00:29:32.345
Sometimes the consumer wants
to return something and

00:29:32.345 --> 00:29:35.335
we refund immediately even
before the item is retrieved.

00:29:35.335 --> 00:29:41.300
Okay, so they're many things we've
build into creating an environment

00:29:41.300 --> 00:29:46.603
that consumers can trust and
feel comfortable, to shop online.

00:29:46.603 --> 00:29:50.958
&gt;&gt; We've heard a lot about what Jumia has
done to change the commerce paradigm in

00:29:50.958 --> 00:29:51.502
Africa.

00:29:51.502 --> 00:29:55.075
And as we wrapped up our conversation,
I asked Juliet how much she thought

00:29:55.075 --> 00:29:59.430
e-commerce would actually drive
development, across the continent.

00:29:59.430 --> 00:30:03.176
&gt;&gt; I mean it's already contributing
to development on the continent.

00:30:03.176 --> 00:30:07.812
There was a BCG report that talked about
the fact that look marketplaces like Jumia

00:30:07.812 --> 00:30:12.263
by 2025 could be, contributing almost
3 million jobs on the continent.

00:30:12.263 --> 00:30:15.650
So, in terms of you're talking about jobs,
that's one.

00:30:15.650 --> 00:30:16.384
Number two,

00:30:16.384 --> 00:30:20.536
you're talking about formalizing
informal retail like you mentioned.

00:30:20.536 --> 00:30:23.298
You're also recognizes another area,

00:30:23.298 --> 00:30:27.039
which is the cross border
trade within Africa itself.

00:30:27.039 --> 00:30:31.830
So those are many pathways and
many areas in which e-commerce and

00:30:31.830 --> 00:30:37.504
companies like Jumia can make a
significant contribution to the continent.

00:30:37.504 --> 00:30:40.105
&gt;&gt; We tend to think of
these shifts as inevitable,

00:30:40.105 --> 00:30:42.730
a byproduct of technological advances.

00:30:42.730 --> 00:30:47.069
But I think jumia shows how much careful
thought and effort has to go into solving

00:30:47.069 --> 00:30:50.591
a host of problems in traditional,
largely informal markets.

00:30:50.591 --> 00:30:53.484
Their commitment to using existing assets,
and

00:30:53.484 --> 00:30:57.936
working with partners who are already
on the ground, has eased adoption.

00:30:57.936 --> 00:31:01.822
Trust was built with tools for buyer
recourse, and access to information for

00:31:01.822 --> 00:31:02.373
sellers.

00:31:02.373 --> 00:31:05.828
And collaborative work with
regulators will help solidify their

00:31:05.828 --> 00:31:09.796
standing as they create their own
paradigm for commerce on the continent.

00:31:09.796 --> 00:31:14.472
But Jumia is not alone, although
the potential Pan African market is huge,

00:31:14.472 --> 00:31:19.457
there are many new and some established
players competing aggressively for it.

00:31:19.457 --> 00:31:22.625
I do wish Jumia all the best
as they seek to scale.

